    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "I reproduced the bug on current main. The root cause is in `AutogradFunctionApplyVariable.rewire_bwd_graph_outputs` in `torch/_dynamo/variables/higher_order_ops.py`, when the same tensor is passed to multiple positional slots of `apply()`, the loop over `orig_fwd_args` blindly overwrites `outer_fwd_proxy_to_bwd_node[fwd_proxy]` on each iteration instead of accumulating, so only the last slot's backward contribution survives.\n\nFix: extract `fwd_proxy = fwd_arg.proxy` and accumulate via `bwd_graph.call_function(operator.add, ...)` when the proxy is already mapped to a non-None node, and guard the None assignment with `if fwd_proxy not in outer_fwd_proxy_to_bwd_node` to prevent None from overwriting a real gradient.\n\nAll 8 permutations of the 3-alias case pass, and the full `AutogradFunctionTests` suite passes with no regressions. ",
